==English==
{{wikipedia|thallus (tissue)}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|grc|θαλλός||young shoot, twig}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*dʰal||to bloom}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK|US}} {{IPA|en|/ˈθæl.əs/}}
* {{rhymes|en|æləs|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|es|thalli}}

# {{lb|en|botany}} An [[undifferentiated]] [[plant]] [[body]], such as in [[algae]].
#* {{RQ:Thoreau Walden|chapter=Spring|passage=As it flows it takes the forms of sappy leaves or vines, making heaps of pulpy sprays a foot or more in depth, and resembling, as you look down on them, the laciniated, lobed, and imbricated '''thalluses''' of some lichens; {{...|or you are reminded of coral, of leopard’s paws or birds’ feet, of brains or lungs or bowels, and excrements of all kinds.}}}}
# {{lb|en|botany}} Any plant body lacking [[vascular]] [[tissue]].

